      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Devas Multimedia Private Ltd. signed a satellite-leasing agreement with Antrix Corporation Ltd., which is owned by the Republic of India for use by its Department of Space."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Devas then petitioned the United States District Court for the Western District of Washington to confrm the award."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certiorari to the united states court of appeals for the ninth circuit No. 23\u20131201. Argued March 3, 2025\u2014Decided June 5, 2025"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Antrix",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Antrix's alternative arguments\u2014that the Fifth Amendment itself requires a showing of minimum contacts, that the claims at issue do not fall within the FSIA's arbitration exception, and that the suit should be"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0000-0006",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We hold it does not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Notably absent from \u00a7 1330(b) is any reference to \u201cminimum contacts.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we decline to add in what Congress left out: the FSIA was supposed to \u201cclarify the governing standards,\u201d not hide the ball."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit based its contrary interpretation on a strange statutory argument and on the FSIA's legislative history."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Personal jurisdiction exists under \u00a7 1330(b) of the FSIA when an immunity exception applies and service is proper."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "61e5766206c58fdc9e8773ca47bd9c43155c62a012d2aa0dfb9a9410d5de43a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-61e5766206c5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the Ninth Circuit required more, we reverse the judgment below and remand the suit for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
